{
  "comment": "Catalog of tools/models/convert.ps1 (contract 'geo', unit F2). 'layers': every model layer TF registers in ClientRegistrationEvents.registerLayerDefinitions (the converter fails on a missing one) with its owning unit (rule R3), the ids it serves (checked against docs/spec/owners.tsv), its textures (paths below TF's assets/twilightforest/textures/, 'minecraft:' = vanilla) and the class whose setupAnim becomes the base animation. kind: entity (default) | block | item (block entity / item models, no animation) | armor (written per slot by 'armor') | source (used by 'extracts' only); vanilla: the layer is a vanilla Minecraft model, use that Bedrock geometry; skip: not drawn. 'armor': armor and Travellers' Gear attachables (bones carry the player's bone names). 'extracts': parts drawn with a renderer's PoseStack transforms (trophies on blocks; worn and held items); 'opChains' are shared PoseStack transform chains (translate in blocks, rotations in degrees, as TF's renderers apply them); ['display', <context>] is the display transform (ItemTransform) of the extract's TF item model (models/item/<item>.json and its parents, read from the TF checkout). An extract with 'item' and 'forms' is written once per form of 'itemForms' (<name>_worn on the head, <name>_held in the right hand, <name>_held_left in the left hand) and gets one attachable with the geometry of every form, drawn in its slot (c.item_slot). Pose expressions may use ageInTicks (0 in the geometry); with 'animation' they also become a base animation. See docs/spec/models.md.",
  "texturePrefix": "textures/twilightforest/",
  "geometryPrefix": "geometry.twilightforest.",
  "animationPrefix": "animation.twilightforest.",

